;; ADT-CARRIER-COLLAPSE-1. Constructing the recursive arm through a `Result`
;; carrier, and the missing sibling of ACR-7.
;;
;; `collapse-result.llmll` constructs the NULLARY arm, so its `mk` is
;; body-faithful and the collapsed field sort ships in a file that verifies. This
;; file constructs the RECURSIVE arm instead, which is the path that would read
;; the collapsed sort.
;;
;; MEASURED: it falls back on `constraint-symbols-unbound`, and the free symbol
;; is `Leaf`, the NULLARY constructor, not the recursive payload. That is the
;; whole reachability risk in one fact. The guard closing this path has nothing
;; to do with the collapse, so a later repair of the nullary-constructor symbol
;; opens the path and makes the sort disagreement reachable. `PAIR-PROJ-LET-1` is
;; the precedent for exactly such a repair landing without anyone noticing what
;; it unblocked.
(export mk)
(type Tree (| Leaf) (| Node Result[Tree, string]))
(def-shell mk [n: int] -> Tree
  (pre (>= n 0))
  (post (= result (Node (ok Leaf))))
  (Node (ok Leaf)))
